        "id": 1916
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-02-26T06:47:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\"demoted to action\"? Keystone rotation should only involve two keys at any given time. What\u0027s the use case for \u0027max_active_keys\u0027?",
      "revId": "8f7b0825fa3b573ad358e4052de37c167bd709c4",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba7be1f8_5c4d1699",
        "filename": "keystone/cli.py",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 207,
      "author": {
        "id": 5046
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-02-26T12:41:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Active keys are allows to decrypt, or verify things. Primary keys are allows to encrypt and sign stuff. Depending on how often your keys rotate you can run into cases where you\u0027ll have multiple active keys that are only there because we need to keep them around for decrypting things. So the key lifecycle might look something like: \n\n    Add new key to the repo as \"active\" -\u003e promote key to \"primary\" -\u003e\n    promote new key to \"primary\" -\u003e demote old primary to active -\u003e\n    remove old primary after it\u0027s older than the token expiration time",
      "parentUuid": "ba7be1f8_3c85d406",
      "revId": "8f7b0825fa3b573ad358e4052de37c167bd709c4",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba7be1f8_bcc2a450",
        "filename": "keystone/cli.py",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 212,
      "author": {
        "id": 1916
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-02-26T06:47:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "that doesn\u0027t sound right. Why would key rotation invalidate the tokens?",
      "revId": "8f7b0825fa3b573ad358e4052de37c167bd709c4",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ba7be1f8_575c0f19",
        "filename": "keystone/cli.py",
        "patchSetId": 24
      },
      "lineNbr": 212,
      "author": {
        "id": 5046
      },
      "writtenOn": "2015-02-26T12:41:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is saying that there needs to be a happy balance between how many keys you allow in your key repo and how often you rotate your keys. So let\u0027s say that you want to rotate keys every 30 minutes and use a new primary. At the same time your token lifespan is something like 6 hours, but your max_active_keys is only 4. This would break because we would have at least 12 active keys at any given point in time.",
      "parentUuid": "ba7be1f8_bcc2a450",
      "revId": "8f7b0825fa3b573ad358e4052de37c167bd709c4",
      "serverId": "4a232e18-c5a9-48ee-94c0-e04e7cca6543",
      "unresolved": false
    },
